8. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS — LICENSE AUDIT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
A full dependency-license audit was performed against the package manifest
(package.json / pyproject.toml) and the installed dependency tree. No package
under a pure copyleft license (AGPL / LGPL / SSPL / CPAL / EUPL, or GPL
without a permissive dual-license option) is included.

Two categories of dependency require specific notice:

  (a) DUAL-LICENSED MIT / GPL-3.0-or-later
      jszip — used under the MIT option. The GPL alternative is NOT chosen.

  (b) MPL-2.0 (file-level copyleft)
      lightningcss, lightningcss-linux-x64-gnu, lightningcss-linux-x64-musl
      (used by the Tailwind / Vite build toolchain at build time only).
      These files are used verbatim, unmodified, as supplied by upstream.
      You may replace them with a non-MPL CSS minifier/transformer in your
      own fork; this repository does not modify MPL-2.0 source files.

All remaining npm dependencies are under permissive licenses
(MIT / ISC / Apache-2.0 / BSD-2-Clause / BSD-3-Clause / BlueOak-1.0.0 / 0BSD /
CC0-1.0 / Zlib). The CC-BY-3.0 and CC-BY-4.0 entries (spdx-exceptions,
spdx-ranges, caniuse-lite) are data/SPDX-list files, not code libraries,
used only by build tooling (autoprefixer / browserslist) at build time.

Python-side dependencies (pyproject.toml) are similarly permissive:
beautifulsoup4 (MIT), cryptography (Apache-2.0/BSD), httpx (BSD),
huggingface_hub (Apache-2.0), pikepdf (MPL-2.0 — used unmodified),
pyarrow (Apache-2.0), pypdf (BSD), requests (Apache-2.0), selenium
(Apache-2.0), tenacity (Apache-2.0), trio (MIT/Apache-2.0), trio-websocket
(MIT), typing_extensions (PSF/MIT), urllib3 (MIT), websocket-client (Apache-2.0).

The github-cli package was removed after audit because its license field
was a non-SPDX custom URL and it was not imported anywhere in the codebase.

Nothing in this Agreement modifies or restricts your rights in those
third-party components under their own upstream licenses; this proprietary
license applies only to the Licensor's own code and materials.

